# CMOS On-Chip Integrated Transformers Comparison

**Authors:** M. Derkaoui, Y. Benhadda, Azzedine Hamid

## Abstract
This paper describes the comparison of two different integrated transformer topologies operating for high frequency applications. Planar stacked octagonal and circular coil topologies are studied to illustrate the good performance. The primary and secondary coils have the same dimensions with 1:1 turn ratio. The simplified physical equivalent circuit is demonstrated to evaluate its components values. Finite element method analysis was carried out to show the electromagnetic and thermal behaviour. Simulations show quality factor improvements for the flipped circular topology. The octagonal topology avoids to concentrates the current density in the angles but allows to increase the temperature due to the great number of segments. The results revealed that the planar transformer with the circular topology offers high performances.

